#!/usr/local/bin/dyalogscript
⍝ Exercises the fff-mcp text shapes ground-truthed against the fff
⍝ source itself (D:\devel\fff, crates/fff-mcp) rather than just
⍝ observed empirically — see docs/adr/0001-architecture-decisions.md
⍝ ADR D11 and TODO.md's Fff cover layer section.
⎕IO←1
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/Shell.dyalog'
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/JsonRpc.dyalog'
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/Mcp.dyalog'
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/Fff.dyalog'

h←Fff.Connect'D:\devel\mcp-client'

⍝ find_files with zero hits: fff's own text is "0 results (N indexed)",
⍝ a different phrase from grep's "0 matches." — must not be misread as
⍝ a bogus single-path result.
r1←h Fff.Find⌽'zzz_hctam_on_ylniatrec_zzz'
⎕←'empty find_files: shown=',(⍕r1.Shown),' total=',(⍕r1.Total),' paths=',(⍕≢r1.Paths)
:If (r1.Shown≠0)∨(r1.Total≠0)∨(0≠≢r1.Paths)
    ⎕←'FAIL: expected an all-zero empty result'
:EndIf

⍝ An explicit `context` line is rendered with a HYPHEN separator
⍝ (" N-text"), not the colon a real match uses (" N: text") — and a
⍝ "--" line separates match groups. Both must parse as first-class
⍝ Matches entries (Kind='Context'), not get misread as bogus new
⍝ file-path boundaries.
r2←h Fff.Grep('*.dyalog _ParseCount'(context:1 ⋄ maxResults:3))
⎕←'context probe: files=',⍕≢r2.Files
kinds←(∊r2.Files.Matches).Kind
⎕←'kinds seen: ',⍕kinds
:If ~∨/'Context'∘≡¨kinds
    ⎕←'FAIL: expected at least one Context-kind entry with context:1'
:EndIf

⍝ grep/multi_grep's cursor comes from an internal file-scan page limit
⍝ (50 files per fff's GrepSearchOptions) — independent of maxResults
⍝ truncating the match count, and not reliably triggerable against a
⍝ repo this small. Test the extraction logic directly instead, against
⍝ a hand-built sample matching the documented shape: "\ncursor: N"
⍝ (a blank line, then the cursor) rather than find_files' bare
⍝ trailing line — must still be extracted, and the blank line must not
⍝ corrupt file/match grouping.
nl←⎕UCS 10
sample←'src/a.dyalog',nl,' 1: hit',nl,nl,'cursor: 42'
p←Fff._ParseGrep sample
⎕←'synthetic cursor=[',p.Cursor,'] files=',⍕≢p.Files
:If (p.Cursor≢'42')∨(1≠≢p.Files)
    ⎕←'FAIL: expected cursor=42 and exactly one file'
:EndIf

Fff.Disconnect h
⎕←'done'
⎕OFF
